        "title": "Multiplying 3x3 Square Matrices"
      },
      "question": {
        ":question/problem": "Calculate $AB$, where\n\n<div class=\"matrix-operands matrix-operands-stacked\">\n<div>$A=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n<div>$B=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n</div>\n\nComplete the product.\n\n<div class=\"matrix-answer\">\n<span class=\"matrix-answer-label\">$AB=$</span>\n<div class=\"matrix-answer-brackets\">\n<table aria-label=\"Answer matrix\"><tbody>\n<tr><td>$2$</td><td>{{field-1}}</td><td>$2$</td></tr>\n<tr><td>$2$</td><td>$-2$</td><td>{{field-2}}</td></tr>\n<tr><td>{{field-3}}</td><td>$-1$</td><td>$-1$</td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n</div>\n</div>",
        ":question/worked-solution": "Multiply each row of $A$ by each column of $B$, adding the three pairwise products.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}c_{11} &= 1\\cdot2+0\\cdot1+2\\cdot0 = 2 \\\\ c_{12} &= 1\\cdot1+0\\cdot(-1)+2\\cdot2 = 5 \\\\ c_{13} &= 1\\cdot0+0\\cdot2+2\\cdot1 = 2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}c_{21} &= 0\\cdot2+2\\cdot1+0\\cdot0 = 2 \\\\ c_{22} &= 0\\cdot1+2\\cdot(-1)+0\\cdot2 = -2 \\\\ c_{23} &= 0\\cdot0+2\\cdot2+0\\cdot1 = 4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}c_{31} &= 1\\cdot2+0\\cdot1+(-1)\\cdot0 = 2 \\\\ c_{32} &= 1\\cdot1+0\\cdot(-1)+(-1)\\cdot2 = -1 \\\\ c_{33} &= 1\\cdot0+0\\cdot2+(-1)\\cdot1 = -1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n$$\nAB=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 5 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -2 & 4 \\\\ 2 & -1 & -1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n",
        ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
