        ":question/worked-solution": "Multiply each row of $A$ by each column of $B$, adding the three pairwise products.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}c_{11} &= (-3)\\cdot(-1)+(-1)\\cdot3+0\\cdot(-3) = 0 \\\\ c_{12} &= (-3)\\cdot2+(-1)\\cdot0+0\\cdot1 = -6 \\\\ c_{13} &= (-3)\\cdot(-1)+(-1)\\cdot2+0\\cdot2 = 1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}c_{21} &= 0\\cdot(-1)+(-2)\\cdot3+0\\cdot(-3) = -6 \\\\ c_{22} &= 0\\cdot2+(-2)\\cdot0+0\\cdot1 = 0 \\\\ c_{23} &= 0\\cdot(-1)+(-2)\\cdot2+0\\cdot2 = -4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}c_{31} &= 2\\cdot(-1)+1\\cdot3+0\\cdot(-3) = 1 \\\\ c_{32} &= 2\\cdot2+1\\cdot0+0\\cdot1 = 4 \\\\ c_{33} &= 2\\cdot(-1)+1\\cdot2+0\\cdot2 = 0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n$$\nAB=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -6 & 1 \\\\ -6 & 0 & -4 \\\\ 1 & 4 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n",
